# Encore — connection profile template
#
# GENERATED from the profile observed working on 2026-09-14, by copying it
# verbatim and blanking only the four fields below. Do not hand-curate this
# file: the previous version was a tidied, commented abstraction of the same
# profile and had silently lost cert_ignore, which cost a debugging session.
# If it needs to change, change a working profile, prove it, and regenerate.
#
# Fill in: server, username. Set the password with encore-install.sh, never
# by hand — it is encrypted with a key generated on that machine.
#
# ONE FIELD WAS CHANGED DELIBERATELY, not carried across: sound=, set to
# `local` on 2026-09-28 for BACKLOG.md item 5. The value came from the client's
# own profile editor, not from reasoning — audio was switched on there and the
# file it wrote was read back. The device half is blank on purpose: the editor
# offers a free textbox and no list, and a blank device resolves per connection
# (R-12). `microphone=` stays empty: input is later work.
#
# If you regenerate this file from a machine whose profile says sound=off, you
# will silently turn audio back off. encore-install.sh refuses to install a
# profile that does not say sound=local, which is the only thing that catches
# it.
